hey what's up my name's samuel leeds and  in this video i'm going to be talking  about what  capital gains tax is when you need to  pay it  and how to avoid paying your capital  gains tax  firstly my name is samuel leeds i've  been in property for over 10 years i've  helped thousands of people  in their property investment journey  i've also written a best-selling  property investment book called buy low  rent high  and capital gains tax is when you buy a  property  the property increases in value and then  you sell it and you've therefore  made a profit and on that profit just  like most profits  you will pay tax and that particular  type of tax is called  capital gains tax now the reason it's  called capital gains tax is because  the capital in your property has gained  value  so the the gained value let's say you  buy a house for 100 grand  and then 10 years later it's worth 200  grand and you sell the house  you have made a hundred thousand pounds  you're gonna have to pay tax on that  money  you're gonna have to pay a fair bit of  tax on that money so you're not gonna be  left with a hundred grand in your pocket  sometimes people don't realize they have  to pay capital gains tax because they  just think well it's an investment  i bought it it went up it's my money but  just the government  always tax you on money that you've made  so it's no different from if you've sold  a product or you've sold a service  you've made money  you've got to pay tax on it now how do  you avoid paying capital gains tax well  the first  obvious way is you get a decent  accountant and you make sure that you  offset losses against your profits so  like in  any business if you've made a profit and  suddenly you're getting taxed on that  profit  you're going to try and find things  where you can say well this was a  business expense and this was an expense  and this was an expense  and you can then knock your profit down  so you've made less  profit so speak to an accountant and see  if you can do that  the second way is if you instead of  selling if you refinance the house  you're still going to make a load of  money from that or not make  and that's this is the great thing this  is the clever thing because  let's say you buy a house for 100 grand  it goes up and it's now worth  200 grand instead of selling it if you  take out a new mortgage  you can refinance it up to its new value  of 200 000 pounds  you're gonna borrow against that and  that money that you take out  you can then invest and you don't pay  any tax on it  zero tax on refinance money i'll give  you an example  so you buy a house for cash hundred  grand it's  uh let's say you don't have a mortgage  on it it's then well and it doesn't  matter if you do or if you don't it then  goes up to two hundred thousand pounds  you sell it you're going to get 100  grand but then you're going to pay a  load of tax  you refinance it you're going to take  out instead of taking out 200 grand  paying a load of tax  you're going to take out probably 75 of  200 grand so you might get 150 grand  you still own the property you don't  sell it you still keep it so you're  continuing making an income from it  you've got 150 grand instead of 200  grand but you don't pay  any tax because that 150 grand is a  mortgage  and a mortgage is a loan is debt and you  can't pay tax on debt  so that 150 grand you can then  invest that into property and you can  you could buy another house for 150  grand  or you could use 150 grand and buy  multiple houses and put down deposits  and you are not paying any tax on that  money which is a really really smart way  to release funds from a property without  paying capital gains tax  the third way to avoid paying capital  gains tax is  if you live in the property you don't  get  capital gains tax on a property that  you've lived in because then it's your  it's your private home  so if you move into a property and you  do it up but you live in it  push the value up and then sell it any  profit that you make  is yours to keep without paying capital  gains tax which is just fantastic so  i would recommend that you speak to an  accountant because i can't give tax  advice i'm not qualified to do that i  can only speak from my experience as a  property investor who's been in the game  now for over a decade i hope you found  this video useful  if you did smash the like button drop a  comment and let me know if you've got  any questions or  let me know what kind of other content  you want you tell me what to make  i'll create the content don't forget to  subscribe you can subscribe  below turn the notification bell on and  i'll see you on the next video thanks  for watching
 

